readableStream.pipe(process.stdout);

// Listen for events on the stream
readableStream.on('data', (data) => {
  // Add the data to the buffer
  buffer.push(data);
});

// Send a summary of the collected data when the service is stopped
readableStream.on('end', () => {
  sendSummary();
});

// Pause the collection service when it encounters an error or a pause signal
readableStream.on('error', (error) => {
  console.error(`Error while collecting data: ${error}`);

  // If the error is related to rate limits, wait before resuming
  if (error instanceof RateLimitExceededError) {
    setTimeout(() => {
      resume();
    }, 1000);
  } else {
    pause();
  }
});
```
This implementation uses the `Readable` stream class from Node.js to create a new stream for reading data from the real-time stream. The `buffer` variable is used to store the collected data while the service is running, and the `apiEndpoint` variable is used to specify the external API endpoint for sending summary data.

The `sendSummary()` function sends a summary of the collected data to the external API endpoint using the `axios` library. The function checks if there is any data in the buffer before sending it, and logs an appropriate message depending on whether or not any data was sent.

The `pause()` and `resume()` functions are used to pause and resume the collection service, respectively. These functions set a flag indicating that the service is paused or running, and empty or restore the buffer as needed. The `RateLimitExceededError` class is imported from the `axios` library to check for rate limit errors while sending summary data. If such an error occurs, the function waits before resuming the service.

The service starts by creating a new stream for reading data from the real-time stream and piping it to the `process.stdout`. It also listens for events on the stream and adds any received data to the buffer. When the service is stopped, it sends a summary of the collected data using the `sendSummary()` function. If an error occurs while collecting data, the service pauses and waits before resuming or sending the data again after waiting as needed."]

