The implementation also includes a mechanism for cleaning up any created directories in case of an error or when explicitly requested by the user. This is done by creating a separate thread that performs the cleanup, which allows for cleanup tasks to be executed even if the main thread fails. The `cleanup` function simply removes the directory from the environment variable and deletes it using the `fs::remove_dir` function.

