using System;
using System.Security.Cryptography;
using System.Text;

public static class AESCBCDecrypter {
    public static byte[] Decrypt(byte[] ciphertext, byte[] key, byte[] iv, PaddingMode padding) {
        // Validate input parameters
        if (ciphertext == null || key == null || iv == null || padding == null) {
            throw new ArgumentNullException("Invalid input parameters");
        }

        if (ciphertext.Length % AES.BlockSize != 0) {
            throw new ArgumentException("Ciphertext length must be a multiple of block size", "ciphertext");
        }

        if (key.Length != AES.KeySize / 8 || iv.Length != AES.BlockSize) {
            throw new ArgumentException("Invalid key or IV length", "key, iv");
        }

        // Rate-limiting mechanism to prevent excessive decryption attempts within a short period
        if (UsageMetrics.IsExcessiveDecryptionAttempt()) {
            LogError("Excessive decryption attempt detected");
            throw new DecryptionException("Excessive decryption attempts are not allowed");
        }

        // Initialize AES-CBC decryptor
        var aes = new AES();
        var cbc = new CBC(aes, iv);
        cbc.Padding = padding;

        // Process ciphertext in chunks to avoid memory overflow
        int chunkSize = 1024 * 1024; // 1 MB
        byte[] plaintext = new byte[ciphertext.Length];
        int offset = 0;
        while (offset < ciphertext.Length) {
            var chunk = ciphertext.Skip(offset).Take(chunkSize).ToArray();
            cbc.Decrypt(chunk, plaintext.Skip(offset).ToArray());
            offset += chunk.Length;
        }

        // Log any errors or warnings during the decryption process
        if (cbc.HasError()) {
            LogWarning("Decryption error: " + cbc.LastErrorMessage);
        } else if (cbc.HasWarning()) {
            LogInfo("Decryption warning: " + cbc.LastWarningMessage);
        }

        return plaintext;
    }
}
```
This code defines a static `AESCBCDecrypter` class that provides a `Decrypt` method to decrypt a given ciphertext using AES-CBC with a given encryption key, IV, and padding. The method validates the input parameters and performs rate-limiting using an external service for monitoring usage metrics. It also processes the ciphertext in chunks to avoid memory overflow and logs any errors or warnings during the decryption process.

The `Decrypt` method first initializes an `AES` object and a `CBC` object with the given key, IV, and padding mode. Then, it iterates over the chunks of the ciphertext and decrypts each chunk using the `cbc.Decrypt` method. The decrypted data is stored in a temporary buffer until the entire ciphertext has been processed.

The rate-limiting mechanism uses an external service to monitor usage metrics and logs for any excessive decryption attempts within a short period. If such attempts are detected, the `UsageMetrics` class throws a `DecryptionException` to prevent further decryption attempts.

The method also handles potential decryption errors or padding issues by logging them using the existing logging framework in the application. The `LastErrorMessage` and `LastWarningMessage` properties of the `CBC` object provide information about any error or warning that occurred during the decryption process.

Finally, the method returns the decrypted plaintext as a byte array.']

