The `manage_sensor_data` function takes a single argument `args`, which is unused in this example. This is because we are using a single thread to perform the operations on the sensor data, so there is no need for any additional arguments.

In contrast, the `manage_sensor_data_multi_threaded` function takes two arguments: `num_threads`, which specifies the number of threads to create, and `args`, which is a pointer to an array of arguments that will be passed to each thread when it is created. In this example, we are using a single argument for each thread, so we pass a pointer to an array with one element for each thread.

