    Record* record = getRecord(key);
    if (record == NULL) {
        printf("Error: No record with key %d\n", key);
        return;
    }

    // Remove the record from the hash table and free its memory
    int index = key % 1024;
    if (hashTable[index] == record) {
        hashTable[index] = record->next;
    } else {
        Record* prevRecord = hashTable[index];
        while (prevRecord->next != record) {
            prevRecord = prevRecord->next;
        }
        prevRecord->next = record->next;
    }
    free(record);

    // Release lock on the hash table
    pthread_mutex_unlock(&mutex);
}
```
This code implements a hash table that maps keys to `Record` structures, where each `Record` contains an integer value. The hash table is protected by a mutex to ensure thread-safety. The `addRecord`, `updateRecord`, and `getRecordValue` functions implement the necessary operations to add, update, and retrieve records from the hash table. The `freeRecord` function frees the memory associated with a record that is no longer needed.

